  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB2-013" ;
  triage:title "quality-mgr's own governing protocol doc still documents the retired 4-step ATM Coordination Protocol ending in receiver acknowledgement" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr BB2-QA3-1789251000 (Final verdict FAIL, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1447#issuecomment-5648745882, 2026-09-12T21:17:10Z; BB2-QA3-B2), reviewed at d2a9b6cc5. .claude/skills/quality-management-gh/SKILL.md:160-166's 'ATM Coordination Protocol' section still documents the retired 4-step flow ending in 'receiver acknowledgement,' directly contradicting docs/team-protocol.md's Required Flow and this same file's own correct atm task close <task-id> completed --template ... verdict commands a few lines above (129/145). Confirmed via direct read: genuine and unmodified. This is quality-mgr's own governing protocol document -- left in place, it would cause quality-mgr to wait for or expect a receiver ack on task-close, reproducing the exact stall pattern the standing memory feedback_qa_verdict_needs_task_complete was written to prevent. Not in SEQUENCE_DOCS either." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
